==Strategy==
You will need some [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark cats]] to kill the Chocolate Wall Doges like [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], as well as meatshields like [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] to protect your anti-Dark units and cats that can outrange Marching Kory in order to kill him.

Although not nearly as important in the earlier levels, bringing [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave Immune Cats]] can be very helpful, primarily in the final stages of this gauntlet. [[Li'l Cow Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Lion Cat]], [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Dread Pirate Catley]] (with [[Talents]]), and [[Rugby Cat (Rare Cat)|Rugby Cat]] can serve as useful wave immune meatshields, with the most easily accessible ones being [[Li'l Cow Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Lion]], and talented [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Catley]].

Additionally, if you use a wave blocker, ideally [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], you may be able to protect your main attackers to some degree. However, if you decide to use Octopus, you will need to protect him <u>at all times</u>, because of his short range; ideally by the two previously mentioned meatshields. However, if those two Cats are not highly leveled, you may need to use four Cats total to protect Octopus (ex. [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk Cat]] and [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]]).

